  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This protocol has an early but discernible scholarly footprint: 3 citations in OpenAlex, 4 documented downstream reuses, and one scite citation that explicitly supports its use. The citing record points to influential neuroscience venues, including <em>Cell</em>, <em>Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences</em>, and <em>Neuroscience Research</em>, suggesting that the method was taken up in established experimental workflows rather than remaining a niche technical note.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in <em>Cold Spring Harbor Protocols</em> in 2007, this article provides practical methods for transfecting primary hippocampal neurons with GFP-tagged actin, including a DOTAP-based lipid method and a calcium phosphate approach for neurons already growing on coverslips. The abstract emphasizes long-term culture survival and imaging suitability, which helps explain why the protocol has value as a methods resource for cell biological studies of neuronal morphology and dynamics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Its impact record is modest in volume but clear in character. OpenAlex shows 3 citations, all appearing between 2013 and 2015, and the citing articles are published in high-visibility neuroscience and general biology journals. That pattern is consistent with reuse of the protocol as enabling infrastructure for experiments on dendritic structure, synaptic plasticity, and related neuronal imaging applications.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Reuse evidence reinforces that interpretation. The record documents 4 downstream reuses, including 3 article-level reuses and 1 biomedical article mention in Europe PMC, indicating that the protocol continued to circulate as a methodological reference in scholarly writing. Scite also registers one supporting citation statement and one mentioning statement, which adds a small but concrete signal that the article is being cited in a way that recognizes its methodological contribution.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding attention data are limited, so the safest reading is that this is an enabling methods paper with selective but meaningful uptake. Rather than broad public discourse, the record shows use within the research literature, especially in neuroscience contexts. In that setting, the article appears to have served as a practical tool for investigators working on actin labeling and neuronal imaging in cultured hippocampal cells.</p>",
